00:00:17.463 --> 00:00:19.380
You might be familiar
with Google's commitment

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.060
to organizing the
world's information

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.700
and making it useful and
accessible but few know

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.380
about Google's equally
aggressive goals

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.130
around sustainability.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:29.640
For example, Google is
using machine learning

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.850
to predict wind power up
to 36 hours in advance,

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.550
turning it into a financially
viable renewable energy

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.650
source that helps
power our data centers.

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:41.620
In fact, Google data
centers are carbon neutral,

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.560
meaning that anyone
who's using Google Cloud

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.960
is contributing toward their
own company's sustainability

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.343
targets.

00:00:47.343 --> 00:00:49.260
So let's take a look at
two of those companies

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.960
and see how they're partnering
with Google to supercharge

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:52.950
those efforts.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.780
National Geographic
Partners seeks

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:58.290
to inspire users to care about
and advocate for sustainability

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.670
with their content.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:02.430
In keeping with their efforts
to be environmentally conscious,

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.680
they moved over their
entire image collection

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.180
to Google Cloud.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.940
In their talk, the VP of
digital products and e-commerce

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:13.050
goes into detail about how they
plan to expand this initiative.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.720
SunPower makes the world's
most efficient solar cells

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.570
and panels for commercial
and residential use.

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:21.240
They're even used by
Google's Project Loon.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.223
Because solar power design
is a complicated process,

00:01:24.223 --> 00:01:25.890
it would take them a
century to roll out

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.800
SunPower to all American
businesses and homes.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.190
But with Google Sunroom, Maps
data, and Google Cloud Machine

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.380
Learning, SunPower is
launching a program

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:38.370
that can create the same design
quote in only 60 seconds.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.230
These and other
sustainability efforts

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.120
have led to some incredible
achievements that

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.790
support our planet and we're
excited to pass them down

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.200
to our customers.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.640
If you'd like to
see the full talk

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.515
and learn more about
environmental programs I

00:01:49.515 --> 00:01:52.097
mentioned, check out the link
in the description below.

00:01:52.097 --> 00:01:54.180
And don't forget to subscribe
to the Cloud YouTube

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.497
channel for more great
Next Rewind content.

00:01:56.497 --> 00:01:57.330
Thanks for watching.

